<title>ZIMBABWE: ZIMBABWE'S TSL BOOSTS FINAL DIV, SHR UP.</title>
<headline>ZIMBABWE'S TSL BOOSTS FINAL DIV, SHR UP.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended October 31, 1996.</p>
<p>	    (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)				  49.0 vs 30.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)				  18.0 vs 13.0</p>
<p>    Pre-interest profit		   301.1 vs 221.9</p>
<p>    Interest received			15.6 vs 14.5</p>
<p>    Interest paid			    31.5 vs 49.0</p>
<p>    Profit shr of associated firms	1.0 vs 1.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  286.2 vs 188.3</p>
<p>    Taxation				   96.6 vs 69.0</p>
<p>    After-tax profit			189.7 vs 119.3</p>
<p>    Turnover			  1.6 billion vs 1.3 billion</p>
<p>Div payable March 24 on register March 14.</p>
<p>Full name: T.S.L Limited .</p>
<p>NOTE:- The tobacco group said with current weather patterns</p>
<p>being experienced across Zimbabwe, the outlook for 1997 was</p>
<p>bright.</p>
<p>The forecast of seven percent gross domestic product growth</p>
<p>should provide a much needed stimulus to the economy and</p>
<p>consumer demand. It said a second, good rainfall season would</p>
<p>restore some normality to the business cycle.</p>
<p>The group said its Hunyani subsidiary was well positioned to</p>
<p>take advantage of this upturn in economic growth with its</p>
<p>impending acquisition of Flexible Packaging. It said a larger</p>
<p>tobacco crop of 235 million kgs forecast for 1997 would benefit</p>
<p>its Tobacco Sales Floor and Bak Storage firms.</p>
<p>-- Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
</text>
